# Testing & verify methodology

**Primary source:** Google's own "Create a testing strategy for Android"
agent skill (`developer.android.com/agents/skills/testing/testing-setup`)
— JUnit4 for local and instrumented tests, Compose Testing APIs (v2) for
UI, Espresso only if the project has Views, Robolectric to run behavior
UI tests without a device/emulator.

**Community layer:** MockK (Kotlin-first mocking — do not use Mockito on
a Kotlin-first project), Turbine (for testing `Flow`/`StateFlow`
emissions), and Roborazzi (screenshot/snapshot testing on top of
Robolectric) — none Google-authored, all de facto standard.

## Standard module layout

```text
app/src/
  test/kotlin/...            # JUnit4 — logic, view models (mocked dependencies), Robolectric-backed behavior/screenshot tests
  androidTest/kotlin/...      # Instrumented — the small, critical-journey suite on a real emulator/device
```

## Categories (separate concerns)

| Category | Role | Typical invocation | Assertions |
|----------|------|---------------------|------------|
| **Unit** | Logic, view models — mocked `ApiClient`/`AuthRepository` via Hilt test modules | `./gradlew testDebugUnitTest` | Fast, JVM-only, no emulator |
| **Screenshot** | Composable rendering at fixed configurations (font scale, dark mode) | Same task, Roborazzi on Robolectric | Pixel-diff against committed references |
| **Instrumented** | Critical journeys only (login, one core flow) on a real emulator/device | `./gradlew connectedAndroidTest` | Simulator/device-driven; slow — keep this suite small |

**Convention:** Do not duplicate a full login-to-detail journey in both
screenshot and instrumented tests. Screenshot tests prove a composable
renders correctly in isolation; instrumented tests prove the real
navigation/DI wiring works end to end.

## Gate ladder

1. **Format/lint** — ktlint + detekt (Android Kotlin style guide config), zero warnings on new code
2. **Static analysis** — `./gradlew lint` (Android Lint) alongside detekt
3. **Build** — `./gradlew assembleDebug` for the primary module
4. **Unit tests** — JUnit4 + MockK + Turbine, must pass before any PR merges
5. **Screenshot tests** — Roborazzi, must pass or the PR must include updated reference images with a stated reason
6. **Accessibility checks** — Compose's semantic tree assertions (`assertContentDescriptionEquals`, TalkBack-focus order) run at least once per critical screen
7. **Instrumented tests** — the small, critical-journey suite

**Closure (qualitative):** no numeric quotas on test count. Closure = the
feature map is complete, as-built agrees, and every in-scope capability
has unit and/or screenshot proof plus one instrumented-test journey if it
is a critical path (login, primary navigation).

## Configuration pattern

- Mock `ApiClient` and `AuthRepository` implementations are provided via
  Hilt's `@TestInstallIn` to replace production modules in tests — never
  via subclassing or reflection hacks.
- Screenshot reference images are committed to the repo; regenerate only
  via Roborazzi's `--record` mode, never by hand-editing PNGs.
- Instrumented tests read emulator-safe fixture data from a test-only
  build flavor or a launch fixture — never from a live backend.

## CI vs local

| Layer | CI | Local |
|-------|----|-------|
| Format, lint, build | yes | yes |
| Unit + screenshot tests | yes | yes |
| Accessibility checks | yes (part of the instrumented suite) | yes |
| Instrumented tests | yes (managed device / emulator on CI) | yes |

